{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>See, You say</b> and so forth. The intention of the matter is that since He made him an emissary to bring Israel up to the land, and He said <b>You say to me, 'Bring them up'</b> and so forth, yet He associated with him yet another emissary from on high, as it is written ״וְשָׁלַחְתִּי לְפָנֶיךָ מַלְאָךְ״, it would have been proper to inform him to know with whom he would go. Therefore he said <b>and You have not made known to me</b> who the angel is who will go with me, in order to know whether I will agree to the matter or not, for no person enters into a partnership in a matter with someone he does not know. And if you will say that I will perforce agree to go with the angel You give me, whether he will be agreeable to me or not — behold, <b>You have said, 'I have known you by name'</b> — meaning, You said to me that it is I whom You have raised above all whom You have loved, as expressed in the verse (Exodus 6:3) ״וָאֵרָא אֶל אַבְרָהָם״ and so forth ״וּשְׁמִי ה׳ לֹא נוֹדַעְתִּי לָהֶם״. From this you learn that to me He made Himself known by His unique name, blessed be He, and this is what he says here <b>I have known you by name</b>, and the measure of the word <b>יְדַעְתִּיךָ</b> will shine before you like the measure of ״נוֹדַעְתִּי״ in its place. Understand this." "<b>And He said</b> further <b>and I have found favor in Your eyes</b> — this may be explained according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Yalkut Shimoni 173) who said: When Moses ascended on high he found Rabbi Akiva expounding and so forth. Moses said before the Omnipresent: ״Send this mission through Rabbi Akiva, for he is greater than I,״ and HaShem answered him that He desires none other than Moses. Now, the matter itself indicates that this is nothing but the finding of favor and not on account of attainment in the intellects, for Moses recognized with the eyes of his intellect that Rabbi Akiva is greater than he; nevertheless, HaShem wanted none other than Moses — and this is a sign of favor. And from now on, how will You conduct Yourself with me by this measure? This can only be because Your attributes are still not known to me; therefore he asked to have His attributes made known to him."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:29.895275209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}